<title>USA: Arm Financial Q1 oper earnings rises.</title>
<headline>Arm Financial Q1 oper earnings rises.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Ky. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands of dollars, except where noted)</p>
<p>			     First Quarter Ended, March 31</p>
<p>					   1997     1996  Percentage</p>
<p>								  Increase</p>
<p> Net Investment Spread	 $  18,374$ 14,155	 29.8%</p>
<p> Fee Income			    5,520   4,148	 33.1%</p>
<p> Net Income			    7,609   4,485	 69.7%</p>
<p>Net Income Applicable to</p>
<p> Common Shareholders		 6,421   3,297	 94.8%</p>
<p> Operating Earnings(a)	     6,416   3,559	 80.3%</p>
<p>Sales (in millions):</p>
<p> Retail				  105.1    68.9	 52.5%</p>
<p> Institutional			 248.6   239.6	  3.8%</p>
<p> Total  (b)(c)			 353.7   308.5	 14.7%</p>
<p>				     03/31/97  12/31/96</p>
<p>Total Assets Under</p>
<p>  Management(b) (in millions) $5,097.4 $4,825.6	 5.6%</p>
<p>(a)  Operating earnings represents net income applicable to common shareholders, excluding, net of tax, realized investment gains and losses and non-recurring charges.</p>
<p>(b)  Assets under management and sales exclude the defined benefit pension plan asset management business of ARM Capital Advisors, a unitbased in New York City, which the company intends to sell during 1997. Including this business at ARM Capital Advisors, assets under management of the Company are $8.4 billion at March 31, 1997 and total  sales are $972.6 million for the first quarter of 1997 compared with $738.3 million for the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>(c)  New assets under management accepted both on and off the Company's balance sheet.</p>
<p>Full company name is ARM Financial Group Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
